\par\par \b \uc2 INSTANT VIEW 3-Singapore Oct exports far worse than forecasts\b0\par\par\uc2 800 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2011\par 02:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Adds comments from OCBC, UOB, updates US-SGD rate)\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 17 (Reuters) - Singapore's non-oil domestic exports (NODX) dropped 16.2 percent in October from a year ago, performing far worse than economists had expected.\par \par \uc2  The city-state's key exports fell 5.9 percent from a year ago.\par \par \uc2  Economists had predicted Singapore's non-oil domestic exports would rise 1.6 percent month-month but fall 8.0 percent from a year ago. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   KEY POINTS (Percentage change, year on year):    \tab \par  Month             Oct   Sept    Aug    Jul    Jun    May \par  NODX            -16.2   -4.6    3.9   -2.9    1.0    7.1  \par  Electronics     -31.2  -13.6  -19.4  -16.9  -17.2  -15.2\par  Pharma            7.8   12.5   -7.1   48.5    1.1   61.8  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  COMMENTARY:\tab \par \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  SELENA LING, ECONOMIST, OVERSEA-CHINESE BANKING CORP\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We see the electronics momentum deteriorating rapidly. There\par is no short-term end of the tunnel, although numbers last year\par were skewed by a high base effect. The numbers were weaker than\par what we and the markets were calling for.\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It is too early to say in the midst of the euro zone crisis\par whether the MAS (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) will weaken the Sing dollar. What\par is more pertinent is, we should look at the Q1 numbers and the\par 2012 growth forecast, although the bias is for weakening.\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "We see a developed market slowdown and the weakening is a\par global economic story. The external conditions are sub-par and a\par weak forward is expected."\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  CHOW PENN NEE, ECONOMIST, UNITED OVERSEAS BANK\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "The sharper-than-expected contraction in NODX is in part\par due to high base, but the continued and deeper weakness in\par electronic exports looks worrying. There doesn't seem to be any\par sign of Christmas orders amidst lackluster demand in the U.S.\par and EU. \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "The U.S. semiconductor book-to-bill ratio continues to head\par down, so no turnaround in electronic exports as yet despite the\par improvement seen in domestic PMI data earlier this month.\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "If NODX continues on this trajectory, we might have to\par lower our 2011 full year GDP forecast of 4.8 percent."\tab \par \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  WU KUN LUNG, ECONOMIST, CREDIT SUISSE\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "Both electronics and biomedical were much weaker. We\par already expected a sharp fall in Q4 GDP, led by the biomedical\par sector, but the rest of the areas are likely to remain sluggish.\par So this is consistent with the view that we are likely to see a\par big sequential contraction in Q4 GDP."\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "Biomedical was very strong in Q3 and that was due to\par cyclical reasons. Business surveys indicate that it is going to\par fall sharply in Q4. Electronics hinge more on the global\par environment, especially in the U.S. and Europe, and confidence\par indicators showed things haven't picked up in any significant\par way yet."\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "Singapore's monetary policy is likely to remain in the\par current trend until April next year. We estimate that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is trading at the bottom end of the policy band, and it\par probably will stay in the bottom half until the situation in\par Europe stabilizes."    \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  IRVIN SEAH, ECONOMIST AT DBS\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "It is a huge disappointment and essentially also reflects\par the global uncertainties and weak global demand. Electronics has\par continued to slump, and the fact that this happened during what\par is supposed to be the festive season demand further amplifies\par the weakness in the global economy."\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "It has actually raised the odds of negative\par quarter-on-quarter growth of headline GDP in the fourth\par quarter."\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "I think for now the existing monetary policy is still\par consistent with the general economic outlook, I think when MAS\par (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) adjusted their monetary policy in October, it has\par already taken into account the downside risk to growth in the\par fourth quarter and the first quarter of next year." \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  CHUA HAK BIN, ECONOMIST, \f28 \uc2 \f2 BANK OF AMERICA\f28 \uc2 \f2  MERRILL LYNCH\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "The data confirms that even though Singapore escaped a\par technical recession in the third quarter, the downturn is\par continuing. It's almost certain there's going to be a\par quarter-on-quarter contraction in Q4."\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "U.S. retail sales are holding up well so there could be\par some structural issues (affecting Singapore manufacturers) as\par well, such as the stricter foreign worker policy."\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  On the Singapore dollar exchange rate:\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  "There's no reason for MAS to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unless the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par dollar risks breaching the lower band. It's near there now."\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par       \tab \par  MARKET REACTION   \tab \par  - The Singapore dollar was trading at 1.3000\par against the U.S. dollar at 0105 GMT versus 1.2968 before the\par announcement at 0030 GMT.\tab \par           \tab \par  LINK:         \tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  - To view the full tables, please go to the website of the\par government's IE Singapore at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.iesingapore.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.iesingapore.com}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Kevin Lim)\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE-ECONOMY/EXPORTS (VIEW 3)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111117e7bh0000r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
