\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Singapore Dollar Flat Late After Giving Up Gains; Seen Stable\b0\par\par\uc2 333 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 2011\par 10:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 <table>\par \par \uc2 Latest Change\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD 1.2075 -0.0002\par \par \uc2 Overnight rate 0.06% Unchanged\par \par \uc2 Two-year bond yield: 0.14% +3 bps\par \par \uc2 10-year bond yield: 1.66% +2 bps\par \par \uc2 Two-year swap offer: 0.29% +3 bps\par \par \uc2 10-year swap offer: 2.16% +6 bps\par \par \uc2 2-10-yr swap curve: 187 bps +3 bps\par \par \uc2 </table>\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was little changed against the U.S. dollar late in Asia after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave up most of its gains made over the weekend as markets remained cautious.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar fell to as low as S$1.2018 over the weekend after U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke said at the Jackson Hole annual meeting that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is prepared to take steps to bolster the economy.\par \par \uc2 However, with no talk of specific steps through a third round of quantitative easing measures from the Federal Reserve, the markets remained cautious.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar is likely to remain in a narrow range amid lower volumes after a volatile session since morning, said a trader at a regional bank.\par \par \uc2 "With Jackson Hole behind us, the Singapore dollar will trade off the euro. The euro is likely to edge higher, which means that USD/SGD will drift lower and raise chances of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," the trader said.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar is likely to hold near its current levels against the Singapore dollar in thin trading as London markets are closed. The trader tipped S$1.2000 support and S$1.2100 resistance for the rest of the day.\par \par \uc2 Singapore government bonds drifted lower as market sentiment improved a bit, prompting some investors to think that the recent fall in yields was overdone.\par \par \uc2 -By Gaurav Raghuvanshi; Dow Jones Newswires; +65 64154 154; gaurav.raghuvanshi@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020110830e78t0070t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
