\par\par \b \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Analyst: BOJ Easing, Japan  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  Are 'Positive Actions'\b0\par\par\uc2 By Natasha Brereton-Fukui  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 11:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--New easing measures by the Bank of Japan and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen are "positive actions," but their impact is likely to be limited over time and they don't remove the "big credit challenges" the country faces, a senior analyst at Moody's Investors Service said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Japan stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday, launching a yen-selling campaign that was backed up by Y10 trillion in easing measures from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as officials said they needed to tame market speculation threatening a fragile economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 Moody's\uc2  lead sovereign analyst for Japan \uc2 Tom Byrne\uc2  told Dow Jones Newswires that the BOJ's easing would help to offset deflationary pressures and to some extent aid the recovery of economic activity from various constraints caused by March's devastating earthquake.\par \par \uc2 He noted that the yen's climb was becoming the No. 1 concern for exporters, now that the quake-damaged supply chain is normalizing.\par \par \uc2 "BOJ easing and MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are positive actions, although they will probably have limited effects over time," Byrne said.\par \par \uc2 "However, Japan's big credit challenges remain--fiscal consolidation and economic growth revitalization."\par \par \uc2 Moody's\uc2  is nearing the end of a three-month assessment period on Japan's Aa2 sovereign rating, having put it on review for possible downgrade May 31.\par \par \uc2 -By Natasha Brereton-Fukui, Dow Jones Newswires; +65-6415-4044; natasha.brereton-fukui@dowjones.com [ 04-08-11 1013GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110804e784000yq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
