\par\par \b \uc2 Asian Shares Mostly Up; Yen Tumbles, Tokyo Shares Climb On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Shri Navaratnam   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 575 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2011\par 04:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--Most Asian shares rose Thursday, with the yen tumbling against its rivals and buoying Tokyo stocks after Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Yuhioko Noda said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry Of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after weeks of warning about "one-sided" moves, as authorities step up efforts to cap the high flying yen as it threatened to damage the export economy as it recovers from the March 11 earthquake and tsunami.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan Governor Masaaki Shirakawa said he strongly expects the MOF action will stabilize the yen's recent moves.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  faces a tough battle in the months ahead against yen strength while the situation with the U.S. economy and possible sovereign downgrade remains uncertain, keeping pressure on the dollar," said Koji Fukaya, director of fixed income and global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar rose to Y78.31 from Y77.10 earlier in the day, and compared with Y77.06 in late New York trade Wednesday. The euro was also up at Y112.24, from Y110.35 in New York, while against the dollar it was at $1.4325 compared with $1.4320.\par \par \uc2 "The market is breathing a sigh of relief for now, but the yen remains firm and investors are expecting more rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  later in the day," said Takuya Yamada, senior portfolio manager of ITC Investment Partners.\par \par \uc2 Japan's Nikkei Stock Average rose 1.0%. Most export sector stocks surged on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , overshadowing news Hitachi and \uc2 Mitsubishi Heavy Industries\uc2  plan to merge some \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \uc2 Toyota Motor\uc2  rose 1.9% and \uc2 Sony\uc2  added 1.0%.\par \par \uc2 Hitachi and \uc2 Mitsubishi Heavy Industries\uc2  rose 2.4% and 3.7%, respectively, on news of a possible merger of several of their infrastructure \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which could lead to the creation of one of the world's largest global players in a number of key sectors.\par \par \uc2 "While it's not certain whether the deal will go through, this could signal further consolidation among the more traditional companies," said Yutaka Miura, senior technical analyst at Mizuho Securities.\par \par \uc2 Lead September Japanese government bond futures were up 0.20 at 142.43 points.\par \par \uc2 Most other regional equity markets were only modestly higher in cautious trade after the recent heavy selloffs amid persistent concerns about the global economic outlook. Australia's S&P/ASX 200 gained 0.1%, recovering from an 11-month low touched earlier, supported by resources and bank plays.\par \par \uc2 South Korea's Kospi Composite fell 0.2% and New Zealand's NZX-50 tacked on 0.2%. Dow Jones Industrial Average futures were up 66 points in screen trade.\par \par \uc2 September Nymex crude oil futures are up 27 cents at $92.20. Spot gold was at $1,663.20 per troy ounce, up $2.10 from New York trade.\par \par \uc2 -Shri Navaratnam, Dow Jones Newswires; +65-6415-4142; shri.navaratnam@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at T