\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Weaker, Yen At Post- \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  High Before ECB\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jerry Tan   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 772 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 2011\par 07:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The dollar was broadly weaker in holiday-thinned Asia trade Thursday, with the yen ticking to its highest levels since Japan's March \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investors awaited a rate decision from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The euro, caught between a hawkish ECB outlook and worries about the sovereign-debt crisis on the euro-zone periphery, firmed slightly against the dollar and yen as market participants adjusted positions, with markets closed in Japan, South Korea and Thailand.\par \par \uc2 The ECB is expected to keep its key interest rate on hold in its 1145 GMT decision, with markets closely watching President Jean-Claude Trichet's subsequent news conference for nuances that could point to the timing of future interest-rate rises.\par \par \uc2 With inflation climbing further above the ECB's target of 2%, some economists expect Trichet to signal a further rate hike as early as June, by using the key phrase that the bank is showing "strong vigilance" on price pressures.\par \par \uc2 Michael Wolfolk, a strategist at Bank of New York Mellon, said that if Trichet fails to convey a heightened vigilance on inflation, it could spark a substantial relief rally for the dollar. Alternatively, hawkishness from Trichet could boost the euro toward $1.5000, he said.\par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.4868 at 0537 GMT, up from $1.4827 late Wednesday in New York, and Y119.43 against Y119.47.\par \par \uc2 The yen, benefiting from safe-haven flows along with the Swiss franc as risk aversion swept through markets. The dollar fell below Y80.44 in Asia, the lowest since the Group of Seven joined Tokyo in selling the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  March 18. At 0537 GMT, the dollar was at Y80.45, off its session low Y80.36, according to EBS via CQG, but down from Y80.62 late Wednesday in New York.\par \par \uc2 Analysts are looking to Y80.00 as a major support level, which would trigger expectations that Japan would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to support the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc also gained, with the dollar at CHF0.8595, down from CHF0.8616 in New York.\par \par \uc2 The commodity-linked Australian dollar -- savaged against the U.S. dollar overnight with silver, copper, oil and gold all lower - tumbled to a seven-session low of US$1.0689 from US$1.0766 after the Australia's March retail sales unexpectedly fell 0.5% from February, vs a forecast rise of 0.5%.\par \par \uc2 The Aussie was at US$1.0739 vs US$1.0748 in New York.\par \par \uc2 The pound was also mildly supported before the Bank of England's 1100 GMT rate decision. The U.K. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to leave its key interest rate at its all-time low of 0.5% for the 26th consecutive month.\par \par \uc2 Sterling was at $1.6520 vs $1.6489 in New York.\par \par \uc2 The dollar got a brief boost from Federal Reserve Bank of Atlanta President Dennis Lockhart, who struck a hawkish tone, saying in a speech there's little chance of a double-dip recession or of the Fed embarking on a third round of "quantitative easing." The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , shot up to 73.196 from 73.11 on the comments, though the move quickly reversed. At 0533 GMT, the index was at 72.98 from 73.14 in New York.\par \par \uc2 Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Rates At 00:50 EDT / 0450 GMT\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                         Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par Dollar Rates                        2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par  \par USD/JPY Yen              80.43-47   80.57-59   -0.17  80.69   80.41    -0.97 \par EUR/USD Euro             1.4859-60  1.4825-29  +0.23  1.4869  1.4805  +11.14 \par GBP/USD Sterling         1.6519-23  1.6490-95  +0.18  1.6528  1.6480   +5.96 \par USD/CHF Swiss Franc      0.8601-05  0.8618-21  -0.20  0.8619  0.8584  -19.62 \par USD/CAD Canadian Dlr     0.9582-89  0.9583-87  -0.01  0.9594  0.9564   -4.47 \par AUD/USD Australian Dlr   1.0731-34  1.0747-52  -0.15  1.0770  1.0689   +9.66 \par NZD/USD New Zealand Dlr  0.7913-21  0.7893-03  +0.25  0.7940  0.7888   +1.62 \par  \par Euro Rates \par  \par EUR/JPY Yen              119.53-57  119.44-49  +0.08  119.78  119.24  +10.08 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Jerry Tan, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4046; Jerry.tan@dowjones.com [ 05-05-11 0538GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1034 1863 28038 4162   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110505e75500087\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
