\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Surges Against Yen As Japan MOF  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By James Glynn and Sam Holmes   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 812 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 06:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)-- The U.S. dollar and euro surged against the yen Friday after the Group of Seven finance ministers agreed to joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen, as Japan struggles with multiple natural disasters and an ongoing nuclear emergency.\par \par \uc2 The dollar spiked as high as Y81.84 from around Y79.50 earlier, as G-7 finance ministers issued a communique following a conference call. The dollar was recently at Y81.64.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the united stand added "clout" to the announcement. It marked the first joint G-7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2000.\par \par \uc2 "We express our solidarity with the Japanese people in these difficult times, our readiness to provide any needed cooperation and our confidence in the resilience of the Japanese economy and financial sector," the communique said. "We will monitor exchange markets closely and will cooperate as appropriate."\par \par \uc2 Japan's finance minister told reporters that market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that occurred from 0000 GMT was from authorities in Japan, and each G-7 country would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their own market.\par \par \uc2 "At a time when Japan is in a difficult situation, it is extremely significant that G-7 authorities agreed to act in concert and cooperate for the stability of the markets," Yoshihiko Noda said.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the U.S. dollar was likely to continue rising against the yen over the next 24 hours as central banks take their turn at providing support.\par \par \uc2 "It looks like central banks will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as their markets open, which means round the clock \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and support. We'll probably see dollar/yen two or three big figures higher over the next 24 hours," said Richard Grace, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at the Commonwealth Bank.\par \par \uc2 Westpac\uc2  Global Markets strategists Sean Callow and Robert Rennie said that with the Bank of Japan flooding markets with liquidity in recent days, "this yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to be successful."\par \par \uc2 The G-7 action was more about preventing a one-sided speculative market than the actual level of the yen, they added. "The G-7 does not like one-sided speculative markets."\par \par \uc2 The euro also surged against both the yen and the greenback on the G-7 announcement on expectations the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will do its part to keep the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  low. There has been no indication from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  yet that it has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "If the ECB is ever to step into the market, that will be during European trading hours, not Asian," one dealer said.\par \par \uc2 After the G-7 announcement the euro climbed to as high as $1.4087 from $1.4020 in late New York trade and to Y115.27 from Y110.62.\par \par \uc2 The euro's and dollar's rallies came against a backdrop of escalating tensions in the Middle East with the United Nations earlier sanctioning a no-fly zone over Libya, setting the stage for a potential vote on a military move within a few hours.\par \par \uc2 The Pentagon was already fine-tuning military options for "serious" strikes against ground and air targets should the White House order them, U.S. defense officials said.\par \par \uc2 OCBC strategists say the current environment may remain inhospitable for excessively strong risk appetite because oil prices remain elevated.\par \par \uc2 "However, some improvement in investor sentiment may be expected near term if investors perceive the latest G-7 solidarity to extending beyond just the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  front, especially in terms of stabilizing markets and providing liquidity as needed," OCBC said.\par \par \uc2 Nymex crude oil futures were recently $1.83 higher at $103.25 a barrel on Globex.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par Dollar Rates                        2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par USD/JPY Yen              81.64-66   78.96-01   +3.39  81.84   78.99    +0.52 \par EUR/USD Euro             1.4071-74  1.4025-26  +0.33  1.4087  1.3978   +5.24 \par GBP/USD Sterling         1.6156-60  1.6135-40  +0.13  1.6190  1.6097   +3.63 \par USD/CHF Swiss Franc      0.9052-57  0.8983-89  +0.77  0.9090  0.8976  -15.40 \par USD/CAD Canadian Dlr     0.9824-28  0.9854-56  -0.30  0.9865  0.9805   -2.05 \par AUD/USD Australian Dlr   0.9937-40  0.9801-06  +1.39  0.9948  0.9779   +1.54 \par NZD/USD New Zealand Dlr  0.7283-86  0.7170-80  +1.58  0.7301  0.7176   -6.47 \par  \par Euro Rates \par EUR/JPY Yen              114.89-93  110.74-78  +3.75  115.27  110.72   +5.81 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By James Glynn, Dow Jones Newswires; +61-2-8272-4685; james.glynn@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Rebecca Howard in Wellington, Geoffrey Rogow and Enda Curran in Sydney contributed to this article. [ 18-03-11 0557GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1035 28038 4163 44462   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110318e73i000d7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
