y by exporters and some offshore banks. However, suspected mild buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  between 30.28 and 30.30 helps bring the pair off its 30.28 early low, say two dealers. "The dollar/baht has moved in a rather independent manner lately due mainly to continuous selling pressures from exporters. However, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's presence in the market, any near-term downside should be limited," says one dealer. Support for the day is pegged at 30.25 while resistance is at 30.35. All eyes are on developments at Japan's Fukushima nuclear power plant for potential near-term cues. (phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0134 GMT [Dow Jones] The KLCI is up 0.1% at 1493.29, after opening slightly lower as concerns over Japan and the Middle East keep investors cautious. A local dealer says there is support from the strength in regional markets and strong U.S. stocks Thursday, but with oil prices rising, the recovery could be short-lived. Broader market breadth is positive, with some investors nibbling on bargains after recent declines: 250 gainers compared with 73 decliners. He tips resistance at 1500 and support at 1474. \uc2 MMC Corp\uc2 . (2194.KU) is up 2.2% at MYR2.73, \uc2 British American Tobacco\uc2  (4162.KU) is up 0.7% at MYR45.32 and \uc2 MISC Bhd\uc2  (3816.KU) is up 0.8% at MYR7.58. Among losers, Public Bank (1295.KU) is down 1.1% at MYR16.72, \uc2 YTL Power\uc2  (6742.KU) is down 1.3% at MYR2.28 and RHB Capital (1066.KU) is down 0.6% at MYR7.96. (ankur.relia@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0129 GMT [Dow Jones] Even though past cases of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have marked turning points for the target \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it's not yet clear that this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be able to keep the JPY from strengthening further ahead as the likely duration of joint efforts is unclear, 