ks Thursday, but with oil prices rising, the recovery could be short-lived. Broader market breadth is positive, with some investors nibbling on bargains after recent declines: 250 gainers compared with 73 decliners. He tips resistance at 1500 and support at 1474. \uc2 MMC Corp\uc2 . (2194.KU) is up 2.2% at MYR2.73, \uc2 British American Tobacco\uc2  (4162.KU) is up 0.7% at MYR45.32 and \uc2 MISC Bhd\uc2  (3816.KU) is up 0.8% at MYR7.58. Among losers, Public Bank (1295.KU) is down 1.1% at MYR16.72, \uc2 YTL Power\uc2  (6742.KU) is down 1.3% at MYR2.28 and RHB Capital (1066.KU) is down 0.6% at MYR7.96. (ankur.relia@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0129 GMT [Dow Jones] Even though past cases of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have marked turning points for the target \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it's not yet clear that this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be able to keep the JPY from strengthening further ahead as the likely duration of joint efforts is unclear, says Osamu Takashima, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for Citibank Japan; "at this moment I can't say whether today's joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be a turning point because this month is the final month for the Japanese fiscal year." Takashima adds "that was one reason why the government and the G-7 decided to step in, but next month we can't expect they will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so there is some possibility that the dollar could drop to around Y75 if they stop." But if any such renewed slides in USD/JPY should materialize, and drag the Nikkei down below 8,000, then it's likely that the G-7 could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again, Takashima says. The USD/JPY is last at 81.26. (andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0122 GMT [Dow Jones] Lead June JGB futures fall, tracking losses in U.S. Treasurys overnight, while gains in the local stock market (the Nikkei is +2.7%) weigh; the contract is down 0.10 at 139.60 after hitting an intraday low of 139.30. Coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen, which are supporting Tokyo shares, also weigh on JGBs. The benchmark 10-year cash JGB yield is up 1.5 bps at 1.215%. (megumi.fujikawa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0115 GMT [Dow Jones] Singapore government bonds may fall, steepening the yield curve slightly, in line with U.S. Treasurys which eased overnight from a three-day rally, a trader with a local bank says. "We will see higher yields today. Some (primary dealers) are covering short, and are unloading to lighten their positions." She tips the two-year bond yield to gain 1-2 bps, and the 10-year yield to rise 2-3 bps. On Thursday, two-year yield slides 1 bp to 0.36%, while the 10-year yield ends flat at 2.30%. (chunhan.wong@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0109 GMT [Dow Jones] The Japan MOF remains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but the size of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is very likely to have been small, say five dealers based in Singapore, some of whom have seen direct flows going through the market related to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Some of them say the campaign that kicked off at 0000 GMT was "Japan's solo act"; so far the JPY-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  is being done only by Japan. Other central banks are expected to act later, during their market hours. The pair is at 81.26, off a post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  high of 81.49. (rosalind.mathieson@dowjones.com) [ 03-17-11 2151ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020110318e73i0001n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
