\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK: Predicted Ranges, Themes\b0\par\par\uc2 703 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 02:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in East Asia today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par          Immediate Range   Larger Range\par \par USD/CNY    6.5417-6.5850   6.5140-6.6017\par USD/HKD    7.7798-7.7984   7.7729-7.8062\par USD/KRW      1100-1150       1050-1172\par USD/TWD    28.630-30.000   28.400-30.950\par USD/SGD    1.2629-1.2909   1.2600-1.3042\par USD/MYR    3.0220-3.0695   3.0000-3.0830\par USD/THB     30.32-31.19     30.00-32.00\par USD/PHP     43.00-44.75     42.34-45.00\par USD/IDR     8,750-9,069     8,640-9,088\par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR mild downward bias. Two dealers said Friday Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to buy USD/MYR at 3.0280, halting its slide. One dealer ventured that without the suspected Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the pair could easily have fallen much further. Some reemergence of risk aversion might provide some support on Monday but Malaysia's insulation to higher oil prices should see the pair slow slide lower amidst intermittent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones technical analysis shows initial support at 3.0220 (Feb.21 low), then 3.0000 (big figure). Initial resistance is at 3.0695 (Jan. 21 peak), before 3.0830 (Jan. 10 high).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD to grind lower around record lows but the downside is limited by expectations of MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with banks estimating that the SGD NEER is at the top of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ''''s policy band. Suspected \uc2 Bank Negara Malaysia\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday will also remind the market of the risks of going too bearish on the USD/SGD. Dow Jones technical analysis shows initial support at 1.2629 (trendline from Dec. 30 low), then 1.2600 (round figure), then 1.2445 (bottom edge of downtrend channel from late December peak). Resistance is at 1.2909 (Jan. 20 high), 1.3042 (Jan. 10 high), above at 1.3100 (round figure).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB sideways trading, muted ahead of Wednesday''''s BOT monetary policy meeting. CIMB Investment Bank economist Julia Goh says, 'we expect the BOT to continue to raise interest rates in order to manage rising inflation expectations, which are due to both cost-push and demand-pull factors...however, we think it will act in a cautious manner to avoid hurting the economic recovery as the combined impact of high oil prices and inflation will moderate domestic demand.' 10 of 11 economists surveyed by Dow Jones forecast a 25 bps hike to 2.50%, while the other tips a 50 bps hike. A dealer said Friday that BOT was suspected of buying the pair throughout the session at around 30.47-30.49. Dow Jones technical analysis shows USD/THB has immediate resistance at 31.19 (Jan. 31 high), then 32.00 (July 20 low, bottom of previous base). Support at 30.32 (Jan. 19 low), before 30.00 (big figure) then 29.50 (Nov. 20 low).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW rangebound. BOK Gov. Choong-soo Kim played financial wet blanket on Friday, saying that the likelihood of a new financial crisis occurring has increased as regulators struggle to keep up with innovations in financial markets. Korean markets are likely to be muted as the NPC in China generates comments galore and ahead of the BOK''''s meeting. KB Investment & Securities fixed-income analyst Jason Lee said, 'the market will likely remain cautious until the policy meeting on Thursday.' Lee expects the BOK to raise its key policy rate. A resurgence of worries over the Middle East tensions could also dampen stock market sentiment and the USD/KRW bears quiet and wary of corporate demand for oil imports. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate USD/KRW resistance is at 1,150 (upper edge of trend channel from May. 25 high), above at 1,172 (Dec. 20 high). Support is at 1,100 (round figure), before 1,050 (bottom of trend channel from May 2010 high), then 995 (July 13, 2008 low).\par \par \uc2 - -\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020110308e737002jp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
