\par\par \b \uc2 PREVIEW-Singapore CPI seen hitting new 2-year high in Jan\b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2011\par 03:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2  WHAT: Singapore consumer price index for January \par \par \uc2  WHEN: Wednesday, Feb. 23, 0500 GMT\par \par \uc2  REUTERS FORECAST: +0.6 pct M/M s/adj, +4.65 pct y/y\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE CONSUMER PRICE INDEX (percentage change)    \tab \par                     Jan         range       Dec       No of \par                     (median)                (actual)  forecasters\par  M/M         0.6         -0.2/+1.2   0.9       10\par  seasonally                                    \par  adjusted                                      \par  Y/Y         4.65        3.9/+5.1    4.6       10\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \tab \par CONTEXT:\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  - Singapore conducts monetary policy by managing the\par Singapore dollar's value against an undisclosed basket of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . A rise in the inflation rate increases the\par likelihood the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will let the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthen\par further at its next monetary policy statement in April.   \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  - Singapore raised its 2011 inflation forecast on Feb. 17 to\par 3-4 pct from 2-3 pct, and warned CPI increases would accelerate\par to 5-6 pct year-on-year before moderating in the second half.\par  \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore said, however, that\par underlying cost and price pressures were largely the same as at\par the previous policy review, and past policy tightening was still\par having an impact on the economy. Its comments were seen by some\par traders as a signal MAS would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prevent the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par dollar from rising. \tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  - Inflation in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been driven primarily by higher\par housing and private transport costs in recent months, but\par economists warn price pressures are beginning to seep into the\par broader economy.\tab \par  \tab \par CONTRIBUTORS\tab \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                     M/M   Y/Y\par  Action Economics                0.8   4.9\par  Capital Economics               0.7   4.5\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2                        1.2   5.1\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2                    0     4.8\par  DBS                             0     4.3\par  ING                             0.7   4.8\par  OCBC                            0.6   4.4\par  Standard Chartered Bank         0.6   4.8\par  United Overseas Bank            -0.2  3.9\par  4cast                           0     3.9\par  Median                          0.6   4.65\par  Previous month                  0.9   4.6\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  \tab \par \tab \par  (Reporting by Kevin Lim)\tab \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE-ECONOMY/CPI (PREVIEW)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|SI    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110222e72m00038\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
