\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Weaker Late, Korea Conflict Weighs On Risk Sentiment\b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 2010\par 09:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD               1.3117   +0.0180 \par    Overnight rate        0.19%    +6 bps \par    Two-year bond yield:  0.39%    -1 bp \par    10-year bond yield:   2.12%    -4 bps \par    Two-year swap offer:  0.81%    -2 bps \par    10-year swap offer:   2.65%    -8 bps \par    2-10-yr swap curve:   184 bps  -6 bps \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar ended weaker late Tuesday, weighed by resurgent concerns about euro-zone debt and news of conflict on the Korean peninsula.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The new wave of risk aversion has driven investors back to the U.S. dollar, which is perceived as a safe-haven asset.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts reckon the sharp and sudden fall in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar could prompt the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to maintain orderly trade in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Yesterday, when the movement was not so dramatic, we heard of some central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Today is a kind of movement we haven't seen for some time and authorities may want to smooth things out," an analyst at a local bank said. "We just need to wait it out."\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar surged to an intraday high of S$1.3159 following news of North Korea's shelling of a South Korean island, but has since pulled back.\par \par \uc2 A trader at a local bank said he expects the greenback to trade in a range of S$1.3048 to S$1.3120 Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Singapore government bond yields were lower as regional stock markets weakened on the eurozone and Korean news.\par \par \uc2 -By Sam Holmes, Dow Jones Newswires; +65-6415-4157; samuel.holmes@dowjones.com [ 23-11-10 0821GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020101123e6bn000m2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
