\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Need Higher LTRO Take-Up For Tensions To Ease\b0\par\par\uc2 1,262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2010\par 10:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0814 GMT [Dow Jones] The market is keeping a close eye on the ECB's 3-month liquidity tender Wednesday given the recent spike in money market rates, with results due around 0915 GMT. The amount expiring is EUR23B but with 3-month Euribor now above the ECB's 1% refinancing rate, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2  feels that a net increase in the LTRO is absolutely needed for tensions to ease. "The next key event will be the expiry of EUR35.7B of 6-month liquidity on Nov. 11 and market participants will be very worried if a larger buffer is not rebuilt ahead of this," SocGen says.(neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0812 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/MYR higher late at 3.1050 vs 3.0950 Tuesday; local dealer says pair rising on USD strength vs emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Adds, Bank Negara governor Zeti saying Tuesday \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent "disorderly" market also causing pair to rise. Tips 3.0950-3.1150 range Thursday. (kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0812 GMT [Dow Jones] Apart from talk of small scale QE, the USD is also getting support from a report in the FT that the G-20 next month is likely to set targets to reduce current account imbalances, says \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 . The bank argues this will move the focus away from nominal exchange rates. "Reducing foreign imbalances without emphasising on exchange rates requires Asia to promote domestic demand, reduce trade barriers and regulations," the bank says, noting that this all takes pressure off the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0812 GMT [Dow Jones] The zloty is slightly weaker tracing the weakening of the euro to the dollar, a trader says. Adds the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected mostly stable ahead of the interest rate decision expected later Wednesday, but may become volatile if deliberations are unusually protracted. EUR/PLN is at 3.9420 from 3.9275 late Tuesday, USD/PLN at 2.8560 from 2.8348. Average yield on 2-year bonds is at 4.77% from 4.78%, 5-year at 5.26% from 5.24%, 10-year at 5.68% from 5.66%. (marcin.sobczyk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0810 GMT [Dow Jones] Firmer French household spending could provide a significant offset to the expected drag on GDP coming from net exports, says \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  economist Tullia Bucco after official data shows a 1.2% rise in French consumer spending on manufactured goods in the third quarter from the second quarter. Says this reinforces upside risks to \uc2 UniCredit\uc2 's 0.3% quarter-on-quarter 3Q GDP forecast. Bucco notes the rebound in September was driven by a "whopping 11.2% surge in car spending," partly correcting the weakness observed in car spending since the spring. (william.horobin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0806 GMT [Dow Jones] iTraxx Japan Series 14 tad higher at 100.5, 102 bps vs yesterday's indication of 100/102 bps. Market tested psychologically important level of 100 bps earlier, but index bounced back due to bargain-hunting by some players, says CDS trader at major Japan bank. Says market keen to find out whether BOJ willing to buy low-rated corporate debt in planned Y5 trillion asset-purchasing program. BOJ widely expected to announce details of program at conclusion of tomorrow's policy-setting meeting. Says "the index may widen again if the specifics are not bold enough as the market has already it priced in," including potential purchases of BBB-rated corporate bonds. Tips benchmark index to trade in 100-110 bps range in near term. Single name CDS deals include \uc2 Keio Corp\uc2 . (9008.TO) at 27 bps, \uc2 Marubeni Corp\uc2 . (8002.TO) at 100 bps vs 105 bps on Oct. 18.(kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0758 GMT [Dow Jones] October HSI futures down 1.8% at 23,137, in line with cash market's 1.8% fall, as sentiment turns negative after cash market stuck in 559-point range since it hit its 2-year high of 23,866 (Oct. 14). Contract trading at about 30-point discount to cash, after ending at premium over past 2 sessions, pointing to slightly negative bias for near-term direction. Volume heavy at 111,636 lots, as traders rollover positions ahead of current-month contract's expiry Thursday. (susanna.tai@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0757 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/SGD higher, tracking broad USD strength vs majors, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Wall Street Journal reports size of U.S. quantitative easing likely smaller than previously estimated, Philip Wee of DBS says. Pair last at 1.3032 vs 1.2979 morning. "Expectations of the U.S. quantitative easing have run ahead and the U.S. dollar is now adjusting itself after the WSJ report this morning," Wee says. Trader at international bank says immediate resistance for pair at 1.3050, followed by 1.3100. Support at 1.2950. \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  MAS earlier said in report it may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb SGD rise as Asia faces risks of strong capital inflows. "Singapore has seen strong capital inflows since the second half of 2009 amidst broad-based weakness of the U.S. dollar and the relatively positive outlook for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  economy. In such instances, MAS may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to dampen upward pressures on the Singapore dollar," MAS says in October macroeconomic review. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0755 GMT [Dow Jones] Sterling got a boost Tuesday as stronger than expected UK 3Q GDP data doused the possibility of the BOE announcing quantitative easing at next week's meeting. However, sterling's potential for recovery vs the EUR should be limited as the issue of QE is not entirely off the agenda yet. "The government's savings programme will only reflect itself in the British economy over the coming months. The expectations regarding QE have merely been postponed," \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  says. EUR/GBP now at 0.8748. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0754 GMT [Dow Jones] Delivering the UK's spending review was an unenviable task, says Wednesday's Taking Stock column, but Chancellor of the Exchequer George Osborne did at least get a lucky break with the timing. (david.cottle@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0751 GMT [Dow Jones] China government bonds lower for 3rd straight session amid ongoing concerns over inflation, following National Bureau of Statistics chief economist Yao Jingyuan's remarks Monday that China's CPI will accelerate in October from September, given low statistical base last year. "We expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will step up its fund-withdrawing efforts via regular open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in coming weeks to curb inflationary pressure," says Shenzhen-based trader with local insurer. Shanghai exchange government bond index ends at 126.26 vs 126.41 last close, short-term supported tipped at 126.0.(ming.wang@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0751 GMT [Dow Jones] AUD/USD has been hurt by the softer than expected 3Q inflation data but Credit Agricole says it would be cautious about getting overly dovish. The fact that inflation is close to the RBA's mid-point target is encouraging, but the signals on economic growth remain very upbeat, the labor market is tight and the support from China's burgeoning economy remains significant, Credit Agricole says. "A modest shortfall on inflation is not the death-knell for further rate hikes in Australia, nor for renewed gains in the AUD," it adds. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com) [ 10-27-10 0414ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101027e6ar0005f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
