\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/IDR Steady; Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Suspected\b0\par\par\uc2 1,280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2010\par 03:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0121 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR steady at 8,920 as Bank Indonesia suspected to have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support pair, which remains under selling pressure, partly linked to Singapore's surprise monetary tightening. 3 dealers say Bank Indonesia bought in an order of $20 million at 8,920, a level it has been defending in recent days. Pair tipped in narrow 8,915-8,930 range for day. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0113 GMT [Dow Jones] OSK Research raises 2011 KLCI target to 1648 from 1580 previously. Says latest move by government to postpone implementation of GST may be precursor to PM Najib calling for an early general election in 2011. Any general election would, in turn, likely be preceded by slew of infrastructure development projects. "As such, sentiment on the ground should remain positive and the good news may help spur further rallies in the stock market for 2011." KLCI target raised to reflect higher PE valuation of 16X vs 15X previously. KLCI last +0.3% at 1501.25. (benjamin.low@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0112 GMT [Dow Jones] Crude extends gains in electronic trading as EUR up vs USD following overnight gains on strong China crude import data. "More speculative money is flowing into commodities prompted by the weak dollar, and investors are not paying much attention to high U.S. oil inventories," says Koichi Murakami, analyst with broker Daiichi Shohin. Adds, U.S. Energy Information Administration's weekly oil inventory data, due later today, won't dent positive sentiment unless expectation of 1.2 million-barrel build exceeded. November Nymex crude last up 72 cents at $83.73/bbl on Globex after rising 1.6% overnight. (mari.iwata@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0105 GMT [Dow Jones] Japan MOF will offer Y600 billion worth of 30-year JGBs later in day with expected coupon at 2.0% vs 2.0% previously; RBS Securities strategist RuiXue Xu expects firm demand due to "steady buying from absolute yield buyers" and even if result turns out to be weaker than expected, "it will likely provide a good opportunity for dip buyers." Says demand in super-long end tends to improve in 2H of fiscal year as life insurance firms typically increase buying around this time of year. Lead December JGB futures now down 0.07 at 143.84, 10-year yield last up 1.5 bps at 0.890%, 30-year yield at 1.970%, up 3.5 bps. (takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0102 GMT [Dow Jones] Impact of latest housing measures announced by Hong Kong government Wednesday may be mild in near term, but right direction in longer-term, says Hang Seng Bank. Notes Hong Kong Chief Executive Donald Tsang unveiled plans to restrict immigration based on real-estate investments and pledged to maintain adequate land supply, providing about 61,000 new units in next 3-4 years. "Given that the ultra-low interest rate and liquidity rich environment are expected to stay for longer, the government's present policy may not be able to reverse the price trend in the near-term," report says; "but new policies to provide steady long term land and housing supply are a step in the right direction."(chester.yung@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0100 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PHP tipped lower on cues from SGD, EUR and U.S. equities; pair may head towards 43.00 psychological support after settling at 43.37 late yesterday, with next support at 42.80, resistance at 43.50. "We could break PHP43 today given developments overseas. Let's see if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," says local bank trader. (cris.larano@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0056 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/CNY expected to extend losses, after USD continues overnight slide vs EUR. Pair tipped to test support at 6.6600 vs yesterday's close of 6.6641. "If the euro extends gains against the dollar, China will have to let the yuan rise in tandem with its policy that manages the yuan with reference to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," says Shanghai-based trader at European bank. USD/CNY central parity tipped between 6.6650 and 6.6700. (rose.yu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0055 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/TWD likely to fall, testing 30.700 support vs 30.960 yesterday, weighed by weak global USD, likely gains in Taiwan shares, says local bank trader; adds TWD also likely boosted by Singapore MAS's tightening move earlier in day. Although tips Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy USD mildly in late session as it has done recently, "the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not likely to reverse this (downward) trend as the global U.S. dollar is very weak." (mason.wu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0052 GMT [Dow Jones] China shares may open higher, tracking gains in overnight U.S. markets, also on strong domestic macroeconomic data like September trade, yuan loans. Shanghai Composite Index faces immediate resistance at 2900, after ending +0.7% at 2861.36. In the 4 trading sessions since the National Day holiday, index has gained 7.7%; but "the pace of gains in the index has come off a bit, and the key sectors to look out for are metal and coal which have been leading the gains so far," says Jacky Zhang from Capital Securities. Shenzhen Composite Index ends +0.7% at 1229.59. (esther.fung@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0051 GMT [Dow Jones] Korea government bonds, bond futures modestly down ahead of BOK rate decision due around 0100 GMT, as investors grow cautious over possible rate hike; 3-year yield quoted +4 bps at 3.32%, 5-year yield also +4 bps at 3.68%, December futures down 10 ticks at 112.65. "But regardless of whether BOK decides to hike rates today or not, a view that BOK isn't likely to opt for any more hikes for the rest of the year will likely spread," providing some support for bonds, says \uc2 Hana Daetoo Securities\uc2  analyst Kim Sang-hoon. But notes if BOK hikes key policy rate, shorter-end bonds likely to take hit. Bond manager at securities firm tips futures in wide 112.20-113.00 range for day. (min-jeong.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0051 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD hits fresh 9-month high of 1.4058 after Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tights monetary policy in surprise move. Move contrasts with mounting speculation U.S. Fed will soon ease more, adding to USD downside, says Kenichiro Ikezawa, senior dealer at \uc2 Daiwa SB Investments\uc2 . Says as pair has breached 1.4050 technical resistance, may target 1.4300 in coming weeks. Last at 1.4040. Meanwhile, USD/CHF marks fresh all-time low of 0.9536. Tips USD/CHF's support at 0.9450 vs last 0.9564.(kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0048 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/SGD expected to test new lows this week after MAS tightens, says OCBC \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst Emmanuel Ng; "they have changed the rules of the game. The Singapore dollar will trade heavier over the next couple of sessions as the market will try to gauge where the new band is." Adds USD/SGD likely to end 2010 below 1.3000, further moves to depend on greenback's moves, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action. "As we go into the G-20 meeting, there is an unspoken consensus that faster rebalancing of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates is called for." USD/SGD last 1.2917; touches record low 1.2886 after MAS policy statement, vs 1.3050 late Asia yesterday. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@dowjones.com) [ 10-13-10 2121ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101014e6ae0001a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
