 40.6 million shares valued at VND1.21 trillion. Among most active, Ocean Group (OGC.VH) ends down 1.9% at VND31,600, \uc2 Thuan Thao Corp\uc2 . (GTT.VH) ends +4.5% at VND11,500, \uc2 Sacombank\uc2  (STB.VH) ends +1.2% at VND16,700. Tips stronger sentiment tomorrow; key index to move in 455-460 range. (phammuoi.nguyen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0418 GMT [Dow Jones] Nomura Securities says BOJ September quarterly tankan result, in which large manufacturers' diffusion index (DI) difference (between current survey and previous survey forecast) declined from +9 in June to +5, is consistent with revision index of analysts' earnings forecasts for manufacturers in Nomura 400 index, which remained positive but contracted between June and September. "Against this backdrop, we think upward revisions to analyst forecasts or company guidance are unlikely to provide support for share prices," writes analyst Ryota Sakagami in report. However, says forecast DIs are below current business conditions DIs for almost all sectors, setting the stage for possible positive surprises ahead. Adds, sectors likely to post positive earnings surprises relative to guidance include electrical machinery, motor vehicles, chemicals, ceramics makers, and pulp and paper makers. (bradford.frischkorn@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0414 GMT [Nikkei/Dow Jones] Office and medical equipment leasing firm Ricoh Leasing (8566.TO) up 2.8% at Y2,088, off high of Y2,120, as company revises up net profit outlook. Shares now up more than 4.0% from 4-week low of Y1,997 on Tuesday when they went ex-dividend for 1H ending September 30. Firm now expects 22% rise in this FY net profit outlook to Y8.1 billion vs previously estimated Y6.9 billion as fall in corporate bankruptcies lead to lower loan provisions, interest rate falls reduce fund-raising costs. Shares now up 13% year-to-date. (kazuhiro.shimamura@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0412 GMT [Dow Jones] NZD/USD weaker after soft building consents data, business confidence 