evises up net profit outlook. Shares now up more than 4.0% from 4-week low of Y1,997 on Tuesday when they went ex-dividend for 1H ending September 30. Firm now expects 22% rise in this FY net profit outlook to Y8.1 billion vs previously estimated Y6.9 billion as fall in corporate bankruptcies lead to lower loan provisions, interest rate falls reduce fund-raising costs. Shares now up 13% year-to-date. (kazuhiro.shimamura@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0412 GMT [Dow Jones] NZD/USD weaker after soft building consents data, business confidence survey but still rangebound, held up by weaker USD, says \uc2 Westpac\uc2  Bank Senior Market Strategist Imre Speizer. Pair last 0.7359 vs 0.7385 early in NZ; "The flavor of the day has been more poor data. Confidence is dribbling off, building activity is weaker than most economists expected." But says as long as USD weakness remains dominant theme, "the Kiwi probably won't fall as much as it probably should." Tips Kiwi to remain 0.7320-0.7340 range. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0412 GMT [Dow Jones] Sensex off 0.1% at 19,948.16 as traders tread cautiously before September derivatives expiry later today. "Trading is subdued. There is some short-covering in select bluechips, mainly financials after yesterday's decline," says dealer at domestic brokerage. Adds, volume tepid, Sensex expected in 19,900-20,160 range. Says, trading activity could pick up towards the close. HDFC (500010.BY), +1.8% at INR719, top gainer, while \uc2 Reliance Communications (532712.BY) \uc2 off 0.8% at INR168.40. \uc2 Hindustan Unilever\uc2  (500696.BY) +0.8% at INR308.20, ICICI Bank (532174.BY) +0.3% at INR1,104.50. Mahindra (500520.BY) down 0.8% at INR693.15, \uc2 Reliance Industries\uc2  (500325.BY) down 0.6% at INR993.50. (gurdev.singh@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0410 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/CNY remains up midday but trims some earlier gains as pair faces downward pressure on pre-holiday bank customers' demand for CNY, despite higher-than-expect