. December bond futures last up 16 ticks at 112.53, 3-year quoted at 3.34% vs 3.37% earlier, 5-year at 3.75% vs 3.80% earlier. 10-year papers at 4.135% vs 4.20% last close. (kanga.kong@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0550 GMT [Dow Jones] Nikkei 225 December futures up 0.8% at 9570 on positive China PMI data for September and better-than-expected BOJ quarterly tankan business sentiment survey results. Investrust CEO Hiroyuki Fukunaga says (going further back in time), futures' recent rise mostly based on expectations for additional monetary easing by U.S. Fed and BOJ. "If economic conditions do not improve after the (anticipated) monetary easing is carried out, we may see a backlash, so it's hard to imagine futures going straight up from here," he says. Puts near-term index target at 9650 and end-October target at 9810. (kana.inagaki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0542 GMT [Dow Jones] Nomura expects USD/MYR to continue its downward trend on expected increase in inflows due to interest rate differential. Robert Subbaraman, chief economist, Asia ex-Japan, says house's year end target for pair is at 3.1800, which he says will have to be revised lower. "In our baseline forecast of no double-dip recession in the U.S., the ringgit is likely to remain strong given the potential for larger capital inflows in light of BNM (Bank Negara) measures to liberalise capital account," house says. Wednesday pair hit fresh 13-year low of 3.0850 vs 3.0915 late yesterday. (ankur.relia@dowjones.com) [ 09-29-10 0245ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100929e69t0004c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
