\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Sets Fresh High As Greenback Falters\b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2010\par 09:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD               1.3165   -0.0063 \par    Overnight rate        0.13%    Unchanged \par    Two-year bond yield:  0.41%    Unchanged \par    10-year bond yield:   2.02%    Unchanged \par    Two-year swap offer:  0.86%    +1 bp \par    10-year swap offer:   2.46%    +3 bp \par    2-10-yr swap curve:   160 bps  +2 bps \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was near a record high against the U.S. dollar late Wednesday amid growing speculation that the world's largest economy may receive another stimulus boost.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was at S$1.3165 in the closing moments of Asian trade, recovering from a record low of S$1.3152 earlier in the day.\par \par \uc2 Overnight, the U.S. reported weaker consumer confidence and manufacturing data. Traders saw the economic weakness as a sign the Federal Reserve may be more likely to introduce further stimulus, pushing up demand for equities and risk-sensitive Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "There is nothing spectacularly positive about the Singapore dollar. It is moving in line with its basket constituents," said Emmanuel Ng, vice president of Treasury Research and Strategy at \uc2 Oversea-Chinese Banking Corp\uc2 . in Singapore. "There is likely to be some official discomfort near the S$1.3150 level."\par \par \uc2 Another analyst, who declined to be named, said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a small way to prop up the U.S. dollar on Wednesday. "If the Bank of Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  later today, we may see a stabilizing effect on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the analyst said.\par \par \uc2 Singapore government bonds were unchanged as investors chose to stay on the sidelines.\par \par \uc2 -By Gaurav Raghuvanshi; Dow Jones Newswires; +65 64154 154; gaurav.raghuvanshi@dowjones.com [ 29-09-10 0742GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100929e69t000lw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
