k including China's and U.S. PMI." Adds techs remain a major drag on overall market as strong TWD may hurt export orders. HTC (2498.TW) down 0.4% at NT$719.00, Acer (2353.TW) down 0.8% at NT$75.70. (lorraine.luk@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0156 GMT [Dow Jones] \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop U.S. dollar after USD/SGD falls to new record low overnight, person familiar with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's thinking tells Dow Jones. Adds, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  near 1.3204 level aimed at smoothing USD fall. "They (MAS) can't change the trend of the weak dollar against Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  but they will try to make the fall orderly. At this point they will continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around S$1.3200," person says. Pair currently at 1.3222 after touching 1.3192 overnight. (djn.singapore.bureau@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0156 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PHP higher early, keeping in step with USD's advance vs some regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , losses on Wall Street overnight; pair last at 43.95 in light volume after settling at 43.90 late Monday, with support expected at 43.80 and resistance at 44.20. Local bank trader notes pattern of pair falling later in session lately, positive investor sentiment for PHP given recent inflows into equities, and says: "The market is also wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially if the dollar slides to the year-low PHP43.88," says local bank trader. (cris.larano@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0151 GMT [Dow Jones] September HSI futures down 0.2% at 22,306, suggesting any profit-taking pressure won't be significant, even after HSI up in 11 out of last 12 sessions. Contract ends yesterday at 20-point premium to cash while October futures end at 19-point premium, continuing to