\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Flat Late As MAS Steps In To Defend Greenback\b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2010\par 10:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par                          Latest   Change \par    USD/SGD               1.3228   +0.0007 \par    Overnight rate        0.13%    Unchanged \par    Two-year bond yield:  0.41%    +3 bps \par    10-year bond yield:   2.00%    Unchanged \par    Two-year swap offer:  0.85%    -1 bp \par    10-year swap offer:   2.43%    Unchanged \par    2-10-yr swap curve:  158 bps   +1 bps \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was flat against the U.S. dollar in late Asian trade Tuesday, coming off its early morning highs after the island's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the greenback's slide.\f28 \par \par \uc2 A person familiar with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's thinking told Dow Jones Newswires earlier in the day that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  "briefly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  around S$1.3204" to smooth the U.S. dollar's decline.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar had hit a record low of S$1.3192 overnight.\par \par \uc2 "They (MAS) can't change the trend of the weak dollar against Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  but they will try to make the fall orderly. At this point they will continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around S$1.3200," the person said.\par \par \uc2 Traders and analysts said broad market sentiment toward Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains strong.\par \par \uc2 "Global sentiment continues to remain strong and demand for the U.S. dollar as a safehaven is likely to remain subdued," a trader with a foreign bank said.\par \par \uc2 In the government bond market, prices were mostly flat with some selling seen at the short-end of the curve.\par \par \uc2 -By P.R. Venkat, Dow Jones Newswires; +65 64154 152; venkat.pr@dowjones.com [ 28-09-10 0806GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1163 1859   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100928e69s000nr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
