\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,002 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2010\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: YUAN APPRECIATION IN CHINA'S, WORLD'S INTERESTS - ADB \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It's in the interests of both China and the world for China to allow its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to appreciate and increase exchange-rate flexibility, as a stronger yuan will strengthen household consumption power, the Asian Development Bank's chief economist said Tuesday. (published 0532 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN'S FINANCE MINISTER WARNS AGAINST NEW DEBT ISSUANCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister sounded a warning Tuesday against issuing more government debt to pay for a planned stimulus package amid growing calls from both ruling and opposition lawmakers for the government to go down this well-trodden road. (published 0509 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA PLANS TOTAL SPENDING OF KRW309.6 TLN IN 2011, UP 5.7% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government unveiled Tuesday a budget plan for next year that aims at fiscal prudence as the local economy recovers fully from the worst global economic downturn in decades. (published 0200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN METI MINISTER: INVESTIGATING IMPACT OF SLOWING IMPORTS FROM CHINA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan is investigating the impact on its domestic companies of slowing imports from China, aiming to gather sufficient facts to encourage China to resolve any problems in the trade flow, Minister of Economy, Trade and Industry Akihiro Ohata said Tuesday. (published 0355 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MAS BRIEFLY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO CUSHION US DOLLAR FALL -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Tuesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar hit an all-time high against the greenback, a person familiar with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's thinking said. (published 0143 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: S KOREA SEPTEMBER CONSUMER SENTIMENT INDEX AT 14-MONTH LOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A key index measuring consumer confidence in South Korea fell for a second straight month to a 14-month low in September, reflecting rising concerns about a possible slowdown in the pace of recovery in the domestic economy. (published 0309 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA OFFICIAL: 2010 INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT GROWTH COULD HIT 13%-14% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's year-on-year industrial output growth for 2010 could be 13%-14%, said Xin Guobin, head of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  monitoring coordination division at the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology, according to remarks posted on the ministry's website Monday. (published 0133 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINESE STEELMAKERS WON'T ACCEPT COSTS FROM AUSTRALIA MINING TAX-REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese steelmakers won't willingly accept additional costs from a potential Australian mining tax, Reuters news agency quoted Shan Shanghua, secretary general of China Iron & Steel Association as saying Tuesday. (published 0325 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: PHILIPPINE TRADE BALANCE IN DEFICIT ON STRONG JULY IMPORTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine imports grew at a double-digit pace in July, reflecting strong domestic demand and economic activity and sending the trade balance back into deficit after one month in the black. (published 0459 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ADB: PHILIPPINE GDP GROWTH LIKELY TO MODERATE IN 2ND HALF \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Asian Development Bank said Tuesday that the economy will likely grow slower in the second half than it did in the first, due largely to a diminishing effect of a favorable base of comparison and persistent uncertainty over the global economy. (published 0524 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: VIETNAM JANUARY-SEPTEMBER GDP UP 6.52% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's gross domestic product in the first nine months of this year grew 6.52% from a year earlier, the government said Tuesday. (published 0207 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SINGAPORE VISITOR ARRIVALS UP 18% ON YEAR TO 996,000 IN AUGUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Visitor arrivals to Singapore rose 18% on year to 996,000 in August, marking the ninth straight month of record arrivals to the island nation, according to a government statement Tuesday. (published 0433 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: 2-YEAR JGBS MEET SOLID DEMAND AMID BOJ EASING SPECULATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Two-year Japanese government bonds saw strong demand at an auction Tuesday, as speculation that the Bank of Japan will likely further ease its monetary policy caused investors to buy the policy-sensitive notes. (published 0452 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINES SETS COUPON ON SEPT 2035 TREASURY BOND AT 8.0% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines Tuesday set the coupon on its 25-year treasury bond at 8.00%, tighter than the yield of similar debt in the secondary market because of excess liquidity in the financial system. (published 0550 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NZ DMO TO LAUNCH GOVERNMENT BOND MATURING MARCH 15, 2019 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The NZ Debt Management Office said Tuesday that would launch a new government bond on Sept. 30, with a maturity date of March 15, 2019. (published 2203 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 KOREA ELECTRIC POWER\f28 \uc2 \f2  PRICES $700M 5-YEAR BOND AT 99.664 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Electric Power Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., South Korea's sole electric power transmission and distribution company, priced a $700 million, five-year bond deal Monday at 180 basis points over comparable U.S. Treasurys, according to people familiar with the matter. (published 0127 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: RBA TO WELCOME AUSSIE DOLLAR GAINS AS ECON BOOMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian dollar is edging closer to parity for the first time since its 1983 float and the move is likely to have the full blessing of the nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , despite the anguished cries from exporters. (published 0507 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =BIG PICTURE: SKIRMISHES WITH CHINA INCREASE RISK OF TRADE WAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 I fear this could end badly. China has been firing trade salvos at both Japan and the U.S. While the motivation differs in each instance, the overriding lesson to keep in the forefront is that trade wars never solved anything. (published 1927 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : EURO RISES VS DOLLAR ON FED EASING DISCUSSION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro rose against the dollar in Asia Tuesday as investors bought the common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the view it may post further gains amid talk the U.S. Federal Reserve may again ease monetary policy. (published 0553 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS: YEN OPTIONS DOWN AS SPOT REMAINS QUIET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options fell Tuesday as the spot stayed quiet due to lingering speculation that any sharp moves might cause the Japanese government to again \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, decreasing hedging demand as a result. (published 0316 GMT) [ 28-09-10 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100928e69s000cd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
