\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,067 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: JAPAN LAUNCHES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , YEN DOWN SHARPLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Wednesday for the first time in more than six years, launching a wave of yen selling to deal with "severe economic conditions" facing the country. (published 0438 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ LEAVING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  UNSTERILIZED - NIKKEI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan decided Wednesday not to absorb funds that flew into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market through the government's yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the Nikkei reported in its Wednesday evening edition, citing sources familiar with the matter. (published 0431 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: BOJ NODA VOWS 'SWIFT AND DECISIVE' ACTION IF NECESSARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Bank of Japan policy board member said Wednesday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will take policy steps "swiftly and decisively" if the country's economic recovery falters and its deflationary trend worsens. (published 0359 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par US FED HAS NO IMMEDIATE COMMENT ON JAPAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. Federal Reserve late Tuesday said it had no immediate comment on Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to weaken the yen. (published 0334 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN MOF OFFICIAL: USUALLY, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  INVOLVES REPEATED ACTION \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market usually involved repeated action, not one-off moves, a Japanese finance ministry official said Wednesday, suggesting the authorities are prepared to continue \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as needed to curb the yen's strength. (published 0426 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN GOVT SENGOKU: FINANCE MINISTER LIKELY SAW Y82 LEVEL AS RED LINE -NIKKEI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda likely considered the dollar's fall below Y83.00 to have been a breach of a critical threshold warranting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the government's top spokesman suggested Wednesday after Tokyo waded into markets to curb the yen's strength, the Nikkei reported. (published 0442 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  WEIGHING YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IMPACT; JAPAN ACTION MAY HELP ASIA -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Singapore\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is gauging the impact of Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which should help other Asian authorities cope with their strong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a person familiar with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's thinking said Wednesday. (published 0532 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: MONETARY POLICY MUST RETURN TO NORMAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's monetary policy must return to normal, People's Bank of China adviser Xia Bin said Wednesday, adding the rapid increase in lending last year created some asset price problems. (published 0454 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA FDI GROWTH DROPS AGAIN, BUT TREND UNCLEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth in foreign direct investment in China slowed sharply for the second consecutive month in August, data issued Wednesday showed, but some economists said a statistical quirk played a big role and monthly fluctuations don't reflect the overall trend. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: PROPERTY MARKET ADJUSTMENTS TO TAKE 2-3 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It will take two to three years for China's property market to complete the adjustments induced by the tightening measures introduced earlier this year to curb speculation and lower prices, People's Bank of China adviser Xia Bin said Wednesday. (published 0524 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA STATISTICS BUREAU CHIEF: CHINA INFLATION 'RELATIVELY STABLE' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's inflation is "relatively stable," Ma Jiantang, head of the National Bureau of Statistics, said Wednesday. (published 0439 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA YUAN HITS FRESH HIGH ON WEAK DOLLAR, FIXING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  guided the yuan to another high against the U.S. dollar for the fourth consecutive trading session Wednesday, after the dollar slumped in international markets overnight and ahead of U.S. Congressional hearings on Beijing's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy. (published 0516 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA: GROUNDLESS TO SAY CHINA MANIPULATING YUAN TO BOOST TRADE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is groundless to say China manipulates its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost foreign trade, Commerce Ministry spokesman Yao Jian said Wednesday at a news conference. (published 0256 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSSIE CONSUMER SENTIMENT, HOUSING DISAPPOINT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Even as Australian consumer confidence dipped broadly in September, economists and markets aren't backpedaling from their view that the local economy is still booming and the central will get back to hiking interest rates. (published 0516 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: S KOREA JOBLESS RATE FALLS IN SIGN OF GROWING OPTIMISM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's unemployment rate fell significantly in August as the private sector stepped up hiring to meet growing demand from both domestic and external markets. (published 0246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN SKILLED VACANCIES INDEX +0.1% IN SEP VS AUG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An index of job vacancies for skilled workers in Australia rose by 0.1% in September from August, and was 16% higher on year, the Department of Employment said Wednesday. (published 0115 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SINGAPORE 2Q UNEMPLOYMENT FLAT AT 2.2% SEASONALLY ADJ VS 1Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's unemployment rate was unchanged at 2.2% in the second quarter from the first, according to the Ministry of Manpower's final estimates released Wednesday. (published 0149 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: PHILIPPINES JOBLESS RATE EASES TO 6.9% IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The unemployment rate in the Philippines eased in July from a two-year high in April as the economy added around 930,000 jobs, mostly in agriculture, the latest jobs survey of the National Statistics Office showed Wednesday. (published 0208 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA EXIM BANK TO ISSUE 3-YEAR YUAN BONDS IN HK IN 4TH QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Export-Import Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  plans to issue three-year yuan bonds in Hong Kong in the fourth quarter to meet growing local demand, bank Vice President Zhu Xinqiang said Wednesday. (published 0319 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CENTRAL HUIJIN SETS COUPON RANGES FOR BOND SALE THURSDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Central Huijin Investment Ltd., the domestic investment arm of China's sovereign-wealth fund, said Wednesday it set the indicative range for the coupons on its bond sale Thursday, which could raise as much as CNY55 billion . (published 0337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WOOLWORTHS PRICES US$1.25B OF SENIOR NOTES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Woolworths Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it has priced a US$1.25 billion bond issue, some of which will be used to pay off a share market buyback. (published 2357 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: JAPAN TAKES ON THE $4 TRILLION MONSTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Those working on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  desk at the Bank of Japan may find themselves selling lots and lots of yen in the next 24 hours. (published 0507 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =PREVIEW: HK JUNE-AUGUST JOBLESS LIKELY UNCHANGED AT 4.3% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's unemployment rate likely held steady in the three months ended Aug. 31, but economists said it could fall toward the end of the year as the city's economy continues to grow. (published 0538 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 15-09-10 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100915e69f000dx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley